<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fante</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fante people, Fanti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fante are an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> people of the central coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast">Cape Coast</a>, Anomabu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mankessim">Mankessim</a>. From the 17th century their states grew rich as middlemen in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trade</a> in gold and slaves with European forts. They formed alliances to resist the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>, often with British support, and in 1868 created the Fante Confederacy, an early African experiment in self-government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fante.jpg" alt="Fante" width="320" height="338" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richter Frank-Jurgen · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Turkson_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
